Adapted from: cmi-am-validation-for-dl-ts-classifiers
  Source : https://github.com/perturbationeffect/cmi-am-validation-for-dl-ts-classifiers
  Paper  : Šimić, A., Veas, E., & Sabol, V. (2025). A comprehensive analysis of
           perturbation methods in explainable AI feature attribution validation
           for neural time series classifiers.
  License: Apache License 2.0

What is adapted:
  - The "Laplace" perturbation method in src/xai/perturbation.py
    (laplace_background) reproduces the behaviour of their
    utils/subsequence_perturbation.py -> class Laplace, i.e. the discrete
    Laplacian second-derivative transform scipy.ndimage.laplace(signal) with
    boundary mode 'reflect'.

Modifications:
  - Re-expressed their stateful subsequence-perturber class as a stateless
    function returning a full-length replacement ("background") array; the region
    slice is applied by perturb_region().
  - The Laplacian operation, kernel, and reflect boundary handling are unchanged
    from their implementation.

  - The MoRF/LeRF deletion-curve construction in src/xai/deletion_curves.py
    follows their interpret_model_regions.py perturbation loop: per-region
    relevance ordering, LeRF = MoRF reversed, cumulative perturbation, tracking
    the originally-predicted class's probability, ×100 scaling, and the
    50%-of-input stop (n_steps = ceil(n_regions * 0.5)).
    Modification: re-expressed as a small pure function driven by our layer-1
    RegionGrid and a generic predict_proba callable, decoupled from their
    tsai/fastai + torch + MongoDB pipeline. The procedure and output format are
    unchanged so their res_utils.py metric functions consume our curves directly.

